 cells; however, this effect may be cell type specific (Zhang et al. 2005). EGF-stimulation causes the complex of PTK6 and AKT1 to dissociate, but the exact mechanism is not known (Zhang et al. 2005).", "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "isChimeric": false, "category": "transition", "catalystActivity": [{"dbId": 8848755, "displayName": "protein tyrosine kinase activity of p-Y342-PTK6:AKT1 [cytosol]", "catalyzedEvent": [8848758], "physicalEntity": {"dbId": 8848750, "displayName": "p-Y342-PTK6:AKT1 [cytosol]", "stId": "R-HSA-8848750", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-8848750.1", "maxDepth": 2, "name": ["p-Y342-PTK6:AKT1"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "catalystActivities": [8848755], "literatureReference": [8848767, 8848752], "consumedByEvent": [8848758], "isChimeric": false, "species": [48887], "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "Complex", "className": "Complex"}, "className": "CatalystActivity", "schemaClass": "CatalystActivity"}], "catalystActivityReference": {"dbId": 9643083, "displayName": "protein tyrosine kinase activity of p-Y342-PTK6:AKT1 [cytosol] Protein tyrosine kinase 6 directly phosphorylates AKT and promotes AKT activation in response to epidermal growth factor", "literatureReference": [8848752], "className": "CatalystActivityReference", "schemaClass": "CatalystActivityReference"}, "input": [{"dbId": 113592, "displayName": "ATP [cytosol]", "stId": "R-ALL-113592", "stIdVersion": "R-ALL-113592.5", "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["ATP", "Adenosine 5'-triphosphate", "ATP(4-)"], "crossReference": [{"dbId": 29359, "displayName": "COMPOUND:C00002", "databaseName": "COMPOUND", "identifier": "C00002", "url": "https://www.kegg.jp/entry/C00002", "className": "DatabaseIdentifier", "schemaClass": "DatabaseIdentifier"}], "isRequired": [{"dbId": 72781, "displayName": "Requirement b